sync-server-placeholder = host or host:port of your own server
sync-device-placeholder = What your other devices call this one
shared-name-placeholder = What other people see beside you; blank says nothing
sync-code-placeholder = Another device's pairing code, then press enter
syncing-note = A change here is taken up within a few seconds.
pairing-note = Scan the code with your phone's camera, or type it into Device sync on the other device. Anyone with it can join your devices, so keep it covered while others can see the screen.
joining-note = Joining another device's code leaves the devices this one syncs with now; a server never learns the code, only a number made from it.
songs-note = A song arrives in the music folder and is read into the library like one dropped on the window. Any playlist's menu fetches its missing songs from a device on request, whatever is chosen here.
copy-code-hint = Put this device's pairing code on the clipboard
show-code-hint = Show the pairing code and its QR code
hide-code-hint = Cover the pairing code and its QR code again
force-hint = Reach your other devices again now, and ask them for any song this device lacks
code-copied = The pairing code is on the clipboard
forced = Reaching your other devices again
not-syncing = Sync is off; turn on Synchronise this device first
regenerate-hint = Make a new pairing code, so a code someone else saw reaches nothing; your other devices then join the new one
armed-to-regenerate = Press again to make a new code: every device using this one stops syncing with this device until the new code is typed into it
regenerated = A new pairing code is being made; type it into your other devices when it shows
drive-hint = Play, pause, skip, seek, set the volume and change the queue of what this device plays
stop-driving-hint = Stop showing what this device plays
driving-waits = Asking the device what it plays…
driving-refused = This device does not let others drive it, or cannot be driven
not-driven = The other device did not take that
