jump-hint = Play this song on the other device
up-hint = Move this song up its queue
down-hint = Move this song down its queue
remove-hint = Take this song out of its queue
show-more-hint = Show more of this queue
forget-hint = Take this device off every device's list; one that syncs again comes back
not-a-code = That is not a pairing code: it is 35 letters and digits, as another device's Device sync group shows it
no-other-device = No other device shares this code yet. Show the pairing code and scan it with your phone, or type it into another device.
no-code-yet = The pairing code is made when this device first syncs: turn on Synchronise this device
hosted-means = Your devices meet through Resonate's server wherever they are, and directly on the same network. What travels is sealed with the pairing code, so the server cannot read it.
own-server-means = Your devices meet through a resonate-server you run, and directly on the same network.
nearby-means = No server at all: your devices sync when they are on the same network, and nothing leaves it. This works with online features off.
